  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Land Systems obligated $1.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Land Systems won 369 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.7M. General Dynamics Land Systems obligations are up 14.8% year over year. General Dynamics Land Systems has seen larger obligated totals in prior fiscal years: FY21 $2.5B, FY22 $4B, FY23 $3.5B, FY24 $2.6B, and FY25 $1.5B. General Dynamics Land Systems remains highly concentrated in Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing, which accounted for $1.6B of FY2026 obligations. General Dynamics Land Systems also recorded obligations in General Automotive Repair $82.4M, Facilities Support Services $34.3M, and Engineering Services $18.9M. General Dynamics Land Systems reported smaller obligations across several manufacturing and services NAICS, including Optical Instrument and Lens Manufacturing $9.6M and Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing $7.9M. Current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date, and the largest industry and year comparisons above reflect obligations, not total contract values in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in FY2026 compared with prior years?",
        "body": "General Dynamics Land Systems obligated $1.8B in FY2026 to date, which is up 14.8% year over year. General Dynamics Land Systems FY26 obligations remain below the FY22 peak of $4B and the FY23 level of $3.5B. General Dynamics Land Systems has experienced a multi-year decline from the FY22 peak before the year-over-year increase reported in FY2026."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are General Dynamics Land Systems federal obligations by market?",
        "body": "Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing is the largest market for General Dynamics Land Systems at $1.6B in FY2026 obligations. General Dynamics Land Systems recorded additional obligations across NAICS such as General Automotive Repair $82.4M, Facilities Support Services $34.3M, and Engineering Services $18.9M. General Dynamics Land Systems also has smaller obligations in several manufacturing NAICS, including Optical Instrument and Lens Manufacturing $9.6M and Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing $7.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
